   "t": "html",
   "html": "<h3 class=\"recname\"><span class=\"kind\">function</span> Bind <span class=\"sws\"><a href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf#nameddest=SWS_CORE_00941\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Core.pdf)\">[SWS_CORE_00941]</a></span> <span class=\"ups\">Upstream: <a class=\"swsref\" href=\"https://www.autosar.org/fileadmin/standards/R25-11/AP/AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf#nameddest=RS_AP_00130\" title=\"Spezifikations-PDF (AUTOSAR_AP_RS_General.pdf)\">RS_AP_00130</a></span></h3>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<pre class=\"syntax\">template &lt;typename F&gt; auto Bind (F &amp;&amp;f) const -&gt; &lt;see below&gt;;</pre>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
  {
   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>Apply the given Callable to the value of this instance, and return a new Result with the result of the call. The Callable is expected to be compatible to one of these two interfaces: • Result&lt;XXX, E&gt; f(const T&amp;); • XXX f(const T&amp;); meaning that the Callable either returns a Result&lt;XXX&gt; or a XXX directly, where XXX can be any type that is suitable for use by class Result. The return type of this function is decltype(f(Value())) for a template argument F that returns a Result type, and it is Result&lt;decltype(f(Value())), E&gt; for a template argument F that does not return a Result type. If this instance does not contain a value, a new Result&lt;XXX, E&gt; is still created and returned, with the original error contents of this instance being copied into the new instance.</p></div>",
   "tail": "\n\n"
  },
